{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794600394,"nonce":"Gs9gqWgMO9UPyH70sGDTGzB5VUM=","title":"A covered window still renders on X11, Windows and Wayland","message":"The desktop runner drops frames for an occluded window on macOS only (f9170ae). winit sends Occluded on X11 as well, and the runner does not act on it there. winit sends no Occluded event on Windows, Wayland, Android or Orbital, so a covered window on those keeps rendering and needs another signal if it is to stop.\n\nOn Wayland the swapchain starves when presents stop (the keep-alive path in the Frame handler), so Occluded cannot simply gate frames there; any change has to keep that path.\n\nNot measured on any of them: the cost of a covered window, or whether it blocks the way macOS does in the drawable acquire.","files":null}]}